plan
meta:
  id: system-overview-dashboard
  title: Operations-first System Overview dashboard with Problems Inbox
  project: meowbox
  status: implementation-ready
  date: 2026-08-23
  owner: operator
  target_surface: web/pages/index.vue
  release_strategy: additive read-only contract, staged diagnostics, no database migration in first release

terms:
  SystemOverview: main dashboard for the currently selected Meowbox server
  ProblemsInbox: prioritized list of concrete operational problems requiring attention
  Problem: deterministic, evidence-backed current condition; never an inferred guess
  Pulse: compact top-level server identity, health, uptime, version and freshness strip
  Snapshot: one bounded API response used to render the dashboard consistently
  DataSource: database, Agent, cached diagnostics or another authoritative provider
  Unknown: source has no trustworthy value yet
  Unavailable: source failed or cannot currently be reached
  Stale: source value exists but is older than its freshness budget
  Coverage: whether a diagnostic is supported, current and trustworthy
  Remediation: operator action intended to resolve a Problem
  LegacyServer: selected remote Meowbox server without DashboardOverview contract v1

goal:
  summary: >
    Replace the scattered card wall on System Overview with a high-signal operations
    workspace that answers, in order: which server is selected, whether it is healthy,
    what requires action, whether resources are safe, what workloads are affected,
    and where the operator should go next.
  outcomes:
    - uptime, selected server, Agent state, version and data freshness are visible at the top
    - Problems Inbox is the primary dashboard surface immediately below server pulse
    - critical and warning conditions are sorted consistently and link to the exact resolution context
    - resource, site, runtime, protection, security and activity data have explicit hierarchy
    - empty, unknown, stale and unavailable states are never confused
    - ADMIN and MANAGER receive correctly scoped data enforced by API authorization
    - selected older remote servers degrade explicitly instead of showing false zeroes
    - dashboard reads remain bounded as site, domain, backup and activity tables grow
    - first release is reversible because it adds no persistent state and performs no remediation mutations

success_metrics:
  product:
    - an operator can identify the highest-severity active problem without scrolling
    - an operator can reach the relevant site, backup, SSL, monitoring, service, DNS or update screen in one action
    - healthy state is understandable in one glance and occupies less height than active-problem state
    - uptime is visible in the first viewport on desktop and mobile reference layouts
    - no dashboard section renders a healthy or zero value when its source is unavailable
  reliability:
    - GET dashboard overview has no write, command, notification or external-provider side effects
    - one failed DataSource does not fail unrelated dashboard sections
    - page polling never overlaps and stops while the tab is hidden
    - old selected servers show an explicit compatibility state
  performance:
    - database query count is constant with respect to site and domain count
    - initial response contains bounded lists and stays at or below 128 KiB JSON
    - API local p95 is at or below 750 ms on the reference production-like fixture
    - proxied selected-server p95 is at or below 1500 ms excluding an offline server timeout
    - no synchronous systemctl, PM2, Nginx or DNS command runs in the HTTP request path

fixed_decisions:
  D01:
    rule: dashboard is selected-server scope
    detail: Fleet aggregation remains on /servers and is not mixed into System Overview.
  D02:
    rule: information order is fixed by operational urgency
    order:
      - server pulse
      - Problems Inbox
      - resource strip
      - sites and runtime
      - protection and security
      - recent activity
  D03:
    rule: Problems Inbox is not a generic equal-weight card
    detail: It spans the content width, has a severity rail and becomes compact only when healthy.
  D04:
    rule: overview is one consistent snapshot
    detail: Web does not independently join several responses into contradictory states when v1 is available.
  D05:
    rule: first release is read-only
    detail: Problem actions navigate to an allowlisted resolution context; they do not mutate infrastructure.
  D06:
    rule: backend never sends arbitrary URLs or HTTP methods as actions
    detail: Backend sends an action target enum and entity ID; Web maps them through a local allowlist.
  D07:
    rule: no Problems Inbox persistence in first release
    detail: No acknowledgement, snooze, assignment or dismissal tables. Active problems are recomputed deterministically.
  D08:
    rule: unknown is not healthy
    detail: Missing pings, metrics, diagnostics or unsupported server capabilities render Unknown or Unavailable.
  D09:
    rule: STOPPED is not automatically a problem
    detail: Intentionally stopped sites and optional services are not flagged; ERROR and violated expected-state contracts are flagged.
  D10:
    rule: instantaneous CPU, memory and load do not create Problems
    detail: They remain visible metrics until a reliable sustained-window policy exists.
  D11:
    rule: every detector is pure and deterministic
    detail: A detector receives a normalized Snapshot input and returns zero or more Problems without I/O.
  D12:
    rule: every source has availability and freshness metadata
    values: [OK, STALE, UNAVAILABLE, UNSUPPORTED]
  D13:
    rule: no N+1 query or per-entity Agent call
  D14:
    rule: diagnostics are collected outside the dashboard HTTP request
    detail: Cached bounded probes use single-flight execution, timeouts and backoff.
  D15:
    rule: current theme and navigation remain intact
    detail: Keep Meowbox dark/light tokens, DM Sans, JetBrains Mono, sidebar and server selector.
  D16:
    rule: visual direction is an operations control room
    detail: Dense but calm, strong hierarchy, precise status language, no decorative charting or generic card mosaic.
  D17:
    rule: charts require real time-series data
    detail: Do not reuse simulated uptime segments or fabricate sparklines from aggregate percentages.
  D18:
    rule: full backup lists do not render on dashboard
    detail: Render summary counts and only the most relevant exceptions; history stays on backup pages.
  D19:
    rule: MANAGER authorization is server-enforced
    detail: Hiding ADMIN content in Vue is not considered authorization.
  D20:
    rule: older selected servers degrade explicitly
    detail: A compatibility adapter may render trusted legacy data but must label unsupported diagnostics.
  D21:
    rule: dashboard work does not repair updater internals
    detail: Failed update state may be shown; UPDATE_BLOCKED requires a separate authoritative readiness contract.
  D22:
    rule: no database or system migration in first dashboard release
    detail: Use current tables and in-memory cached diagnostics; add an index only after query-plan evidence and in a separate Prisma migration.
  D23:
    rule: no layout customization in first release
    detail: One carefully designed hierarchy prevents per-user layouts from hiding urgent information.
  D24:
    rule: all issue text is safe for UI
    detail: Sanitize, redact and truncate source errors; never expose secrets, raw logs, commands or credential-bearing URLs.
  D25:
    rule: diagnostics coverage is visible
    detail: Unsupported Nginx drift, DNS drift or update readiness is shown as unsupported capability, not silently omitted or fabricated.
  D26:
    rule: existing page remains rollback fallback during rollout
    detail: Replace it only after contract, role, compatibility and visual acceptance tests pass.

non_goals:
  - fleet-wide aggregation across master and all slave servers
  - replacing /monitoring, /backups, /ssl, /services, /activity or /servers detail pages
  - arbitrary drag-and-drop dashboard configuration
  - alert acknowledgement, assignment, snooze or incident management workflow
  - executing destructive or restart actions directly from the first Problems Inbox release
  - using dashboard GET requests to probe external DNS providers
  - using dashboard GET requests to run systemctl, pm2, nginx or filesystem scans
  - redesigning the full Meowbox navigation or global design system
  - migration-updater hardening or changing update transaction semantics
  - claiming HTTP uptime from aggregate values without real HealthCheckPing samples
  - treating manually managed files outside Meowbox ownership as configuration drift

current_state:
  page:
    file: web/pages/index.vue
    problems:
      - monolithic page combines template, data orchestration and styling
      - every section has similar visual weight
      - uptime is buried in the last system card
      - quick actions consume prime space without problem context
      - backup rows grow with every site
      - fetch failures are swallowed and appear as empty data
      - metrics, summary and sites requests may represent different moments
  backend:
    endpoint: GET /dashboard/summary
    limitations:
      - ADMIN-only despite site pages supporting MANAGER scope
      - latest backup lookup performs one query per site
      - service status runs system commands in request path
      - missing and stopped services are not reliably distinguished
      - no source availability or freshness contract
      - no endpoint contract tests
  metrics:
    findings:
      - /system/metrics does not return the disk and network shape expected by current page
      - Agent monitoring already receives richer CPU, memory, disk and network values
      - latest monitoring normalization currently drops useful hostname, uptime, load and multi-disk fields
      - health page uses generated visual segments that are not real samples
  operations:
    findings:
      - Operation is durable and contains status, type, progress, step, timestamps and error
      - API exposes operation by ID but not a bounded scoped recent list for dashboard
  compatibility:
    finding: Web may proxy dashboard calls to a selected remote server running an older Meowbox version.

information_architecture:
  desktop_grid:
    columns: 12
    max_width: preserve current 1400px content maximum
    gap: use existing spacing scale with 16px compact section gaps
    rows:
      R01:
        component: ServerPulse
        span: 12
      R02:
        component: ProblemsInbox
        span: 12
      R03:
        component: ResourceStrip
        span: 12
      R04:
        left:
          component: SitesPanel
          span: 8
        right:
          component: RuntimePanel
          span: 4
      R05:
        left:
          component: ProtectionPanel
          span: 8
        right:
          component: SecurityPanel
          span: 4
      R06:
        component: ActivityPanel
        span: 12
  tablet_grid:
    columns: 8
    rules:
      - pulse, inbox and resources span 8
      - sites and protection span 8
      - runtime and security each span 4 when width permits
      - activity spans 8
  mobile_grid:
    columns: 1
    order: same as operational hierarchy
    rules:
      - pulse is compact but uptime remains visible
      - Problems Inbox precedes resource metrics
      - resources use two columns at 360px or wider and one below 360px
      - tables become semantic stacked rows, not horizontal-scroll desktop tables
      - primary tap targets are at least 44px

visual_language:
  direction: industrial utilitarian operations control room
  surfaces:
    - use existing background and border tokens
    - use one base panel treatment; hierarchy comes from structure, spacing and status rail
    - avoid nested cards for every scalar value
    - avoid gradients, glass effects, decorative shadows and oversized rounded pills
  typography:
    labels: DM Sans
    metrics: JetBrains Mono with tabular numerals
    hierarchy:
      - one page title
      - compact section headings with counts and one contextual action
      - metric value first, unit and interpretation second
  status_encoding:
    rules:
      - color is never the only signal
      - every state has icon, text label and accessible name
      - red is reserved for current critical conditions
      - amber is reserved for actionable warnings
      - neutral gray means unknown, unsupported or intentionally inactive
      - green appears only when a source positively confirms healthy state
  motion:
    duration_ms: 120..180
    allowed:
      - metric value transition without count-up animation
      - inbox expand and collapse
      - refresh indicator
    forbidden:
      - looping status animation
      - pulsing healthy badges
      - animated decorative charts
    reduced_motion: disable non-essential transitions under prefers-reduced-motion

components:
  ServerPulse:
    content_order:
      - selected server display name and connection state
      - overall state label derived from active Problems and source coverage
      - uptime
      - Agent state and last seen
      - installed Meowbox version and update state for ADMIN
      - last successful dashboard refresh
    actions:
      primary: Create site for roles allowed by existing site-creation policy
      secondary: manual refresh
    behavior:
      - server switching keeps old content visually marked stale until new server snapshot succeeds
      - never relabel previous server data as belonging to newly selected server
      - offline selected server replaces all server data with explicit offline state

  ProblemsInbox:
    active_state:
      summary: severity counts plus total active Problems
      initial_items: 6
      maximum_response_items: 100
      overflow: open an accessible dialog containing the bounded complete response list
      grouping: no grouping in initial list; optional category filters exist only in dialog
      sort: severity rank ascending, occurredAt descending with null last, code ascending, id ascending
    healthy_state:
      height: compact one-row confirmation
      required_text: No confirmed problems
      caveat: show stale, unavailable or unsupported source count beside healthy text
    item_layout:
      - severity icon and label
      - concise title
      - one-line sanitized summary
      - entity label and observed time
      - one contextual action
    interaction:
      - entire row is not a hidden button
      - action uses an explicit link label such as Open SSL or Open backup
      - keyboard focus order follows visual order
      - opening and closing dialog restores focus

  ResourceStrip:
    primary_metrics:
      - CPU utilization
      - memory used and total
      - root disk used and free
      - load average normalized by CPU core count
    secondary_metrics:
      - network receive and transmit rate
      - additional mounted disks summarized as worst utilization plus count
    rules:
      - current value includes collectedAt age
      - progress bars use clamped 0..100 display values but preserve validation errors as Unknown
      - sparkline appears only when real history contains at least two samples
      - no Problem is generated from one CPU, memory or load sample

  SitesPanel:
    header:
      - total sites
      - running count
      - error count
      - deploying count
      - total managed domains
    rows:
      priority: error, active operation, deploying, recently changed
      maximum: 8
      content:
        - site display name and primary domain
        - site state plus affected domain count
        - real availability percentage only when samples exist
        - direct link to site
    empty_state: Create the first site when role permits; otherwise No sites assigned.
    forbidden:
      - treating no health pings as 100 percent uptime
      - listing every healthy site

  RuntimePanel:
    active_operations:
      maximum: 5
      content: operation type, target, progress, current step, elapsed time
      rules:
        - active operations are context, not Problems by default
        - recently failed operations become Problems through detector rules
    services:
      scope: ADMIN core server services and site services relevant to selected rows
      maximum: 8
      content: installed state, expected state, actual state, last checked
      rules:
        - not installed is distinct from stopped
        - optional not-installed database engines are neutral
        - only expected-running but inactive or ERROR services generate Problems

  ProtectionPanel:
    backup_block:
      - protected site count versus eligible site count
      - most recent successful backup time
      - failed backup count in last 24 hours
      - overdue schedule count
      - active backup count
      - last Restic integrity-check state when configured
    ssl_block:
      - valid certificate count
      - expiring certificate count
      - expired or error count
      - nearest expiry domain and days remaining
    rules:
      - show summaries and exceptions only
      - full histories remain on dedicated pages

  SecurityPanel:
    visibility: ADMIN only
    content:
      - failed login count in last 24 hours
      - active session count
      - last successful login time and actor when safe
      - firewall or allowlist summary only if an authoritative current source exists
    rules:
      - one failed login is not automatically a Problem
      - no IP address, token, raw user agent or sensitive audit payload is exposed in compact dashboard rows

  ActivityPanel:
    maximum: 8
    content:
      - timestamp
      - safe actor label
      - action label
      - target label
      - result state when available
    rules:
      - full audit details remain on /activity
      - no raw metadata JSON

shared_contract:
  location: shared/src/dashboard.ts
  export_from: shared/src/index.ts
  DashboardOverview:
    fields:
      contractVersion: literal 1
      generatedAt: ISO-8601 UTC string
      role: ADMIN or MANAGER
      server: DashboardServerPulse
      overall: DashboardOverallState
      problems: DashboardProblemCollection
      resources: DashboardResourceSection
      sites: DashboardSitesSection
      runtime: DashboardRuntimeSection
      protection: DashboardProtectionSection
      security: DashboardSecuritySection or null
      activity: DashboardActivitySection
      capabilities: DashboardCapabilities
  DashboardSourceState:
    fields:
      availability: OK or STALE or UNAVAILABLE or UNSUPPORTED
      observedAt: ISO-8601 UTC string or null
      staleAfterSeconds: non-negative integer or null
      message: safe user-facing string or null
  DashboardOverallState:
    fields:
      state: HEALTHY or ATTENTION or CRITICAL or UNKNOWN
      criticalCount: non-negative integer
      warningCount: non-negative integer
      infoCount: non-negative integer
      degradedSourceCount: non-negative integer
    derivation:
      CRITICAL: at least one critical Problem
      ATTENTION: no critical Problem and at least one warning Problem
      HEALTHY: no critical or warning Problem and all required sources are OK
      UNKNOWN: no critical or warning Problem but at least one required source is not OK
  DashboardProblem:
    fields:
      id: deterministic string from code, entity kind and stable entity ID
      code: DashboardProblemCode
      severity: CRITICAL or WARNING or INFO
      category: SYSTEM or AGENT or SITE or SERVICE or BACKUP or SSL or OPERATION or SECURITY or UPDATE or DNS
      title: safe string, maximum 100 characters
      summary: safe string, maximum 240 characters
      entity:
        kind: SERVER or SITE or DOMAIN or SERVICE or BACKUP or CERTIFICATE or OPERATION or DNS_PROVIDER
        id: stable entity ID or null for server singleton
        label: safe string, maximum 120 characters
      occurredAt: ISO-8601 UTC string or null
      observedAt: ISO-8601 UTC string
      action: DashboardProblemAction or null
  DashboardProblemAction:
    fields:
      kind: NAVIGATE
      target: MONITORING or SITES or SITE or SERVICES or BACKUPS or SSL or DNS or UPDATES or ACTIVITY
      entityId: stable ID or null
      label: safe localized label key
  DashboardProblemCollection:
    fields:
      total: non-negative integer
      critical: non-negative integer
      warning: non-negative integer
      info: non-negative integer
      truncated: boolean
      items: DashboardProblem array with maximum 100
  DashboardCapabilities:
    fields:
      overviewV1: boolean
      nginxValidation: SUPPORTED or UNSUPPORTED
      nginxDrift: SUPPORTED or UNSUPPORTED
      dnsDrift: SUPPORTED or UNSUPPORTED
      pm2Diagnostics: SUPPORTED or UNSUPPORTED
      updateReadiness: SUPPORTED or UNSUPPORTED
  section_contract:
    rule: every section starts with source DashboardSourceState and contains bounded summary plus bounded items
  validation:
    - API constructs the shared types without any casts to unknown response shapes
    - Web treats response as untrusted and validates contractVersion and required discriminants
    - invalid section data degrades only that section to UNAVAILABLE

role_scope:
  ADMIN:
    data:
      - full server pulse, Agent, resources and core services
      - all sites and domains on selected server
      - all backup, SSL, operations, security, DNS and update summaries
    actions:
      - all allowlisted navigation targets
  MANAGER:
    data:
      - owned sites and their domains
      - owned-site availability, application state, SSL and activity
      - owned-site operations visible under existing ownership rules
      - backup data only if existing product permissions explicitly permit it
    hidden:
      - host resource values
      - Agent diagnostics
      - core service state
      - other users and sites
      - global security, DNS provider credentials/state and panel update state
    actions:
      - only destinations already authorized for that manager
  enforcement:
    - remove controller-wide ADMIN restriction from the new endpoint only
    - read user ID and role from authenticated principal
    - apply ownership predicates inside each scoped query
    - do not fetch ADMIN-only data and discard it after serialization
    - contract tests prove absence, not merely nulling, of unauthorized entity data

problem_detection:
  pipeline:
    - collect normalized bounded source snapshot
    - validate source freshness and availability
    - run independent pure detectors
    - sanitize and truncate generated text
    - deduplicate by deterministic ID
    - sort by fixed severity and time rules
    - count complete result before applying response cap
  isolation:
    - one detector exception becomes DATA_SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE for its source
    - detector exceptions are logged once with correlation ID and no secrets
    - other detectors continue
  no_side_effects:
    - no notification dispatch
    - no audit mutation
    - no status repair
    - no backup or SSL launch
    - no process or service restart

problem_codes:
  agent:
    AGENT_OFFLINE:
      condition: Agent has no active connection after disconnect grace period
      severity: CRITICAL after 120 seconds, WARNING from 30 through 119 seconds
      action: MONITORING
    METRICS_STALE:
      condition: latest Agent metrics age exceeds freshness threshold while Agent is connected
      severity: WARNING after 45 seconds, CRITICAL after 120 seconds
      action: MONITORING
  system:
    DISK_USAGE_WARNING:
      condition: managed filesystem usage is at least 80 percent or available bytes are at most 5 GiB
      severity: WARNING
      action: MONITORING
    DISK_USAGE_CRITICAL:
      condition: managed filesystem usage is at least 95 percent or available bytes are at most 2 GiB
      severity: CRITICAL
      action: MONITORING
    NGINX_CONFIG_INVALID:
      condition: latest cached nginx -t result is confirmed failed
      severity: CRITICAL
      action: SERVICES
    NGINX_MANAGED_CONFIG_DRIFT:
      condition: at least one Meowbox-owned expected file is missing or its SHA-256 differs from canonical rendered content
      severity: WARNING when nginx -t passes, CRITICAL when nginx -t also fails
      action: SERVICES
  service:
    CORE_SERVICE_INACTIVE:
      condition: installed service declared expected-running is inactive or failed
      severity: CRITICAL for Nginx and active database dependency, WARNING for other expected services
      action: SERVICES
    PM2_PROCESS_UNHEALTHY:
      condition: expected managed process exists but PM2 reports errored, stopped or unknown outside an active operation grace period
      severity: CRITICAL for Meowbox API or Agent, WARNING for site process
      action: SERVICES or SITE according to entity
    PM2_PROCESS_MISSING:
      condition: a configured expected process is absent from the relevant PM2 daemon outside deployment grace period
      severity: WARNING
      action: SITE
  site:
    SITE_ERROR:
      condition: Site.status equals ERROR
      severity: CRITICAL
      action: SITE
    DOMAIN_APPLICATION_ERROR:
      condition: SiteDomain.appStatus equals ERROR
      severity: CRITICAL
      action: SITE
    SITE_UNAVAILABLE:
      condition: real recent HealthCheckPing samples satisfy existing outage policy
      severity: CRITICAL
      action: SITE
      guard: zero samples yields Unknown, never SITE_UNAVAILABLE and never healthy
  backup:
    BACKUP_LATEST_FAILED:
      condition: latest completed attempt for an enabled protection target failed
      severity: CRITICAL when no later success exists inside expected window, otherwise WARNING
      action: BACKUPS
    BACKUP_COVERAGE_GAP:
      condition: one or more eligible sites have neither enabled per-site config nor applicable enabled global schedule
      severity: WARNING
      aggregation: one Problem with affected count, not one row per site
      action: BACKUPS
    BACKUP_OVERDUE:
      condition: latest success is later than computed next expected schedule plus grace
      severity: WARNING, CRITICAL after two missed expected executions
      action: BACKUPS
      schedule_rules:
        - use an explicit direct cron library dependency, not an undeclared transitive package
        - use server timezone consistently with scheduler
        - invalid schedule is a separate configuration warning
        - grace is max of 15 minutes or 25 percent of expected interval
    BACKUP_REPOSITORY_CHECK_FAILED:
      condition: latest configured ResticCheck is complete and success is false
      severity: WARNING
      action: BACKUPS
  ssl:
    SSL_ERROR:
      condition: certificate status is an explicit error state
      severity: CRITICAL
      action: SSL
    SSL_EXPIRED:
      condition: expiresAt is earlier than generatedAt or explicit status is expired
      severity: CRITICAL
      action: SSL
    SSL_EXPIRING_CRITICAL:
      condition: daysRemaining is from 0 through 3
      severity: CRITICAL
      action: SSL
    SSL_EXPIRING_WARNING:
      condition: daysRemaining is from 4 through 14
      severity: WARNING
      action: SSL
    SSL_EXPECTED_BUT_UNKNOWN:
      condition: HTTPS is expected but certificate state or expiry is absent
      severity: WARNING
      action: SSL
  operation:
    OPERATION_RECENTLY_FAILED:
      condition: latest terminal operation for an entity failed within 24 hours and no later successful equivalent operation exists
      severity: WARNING, CRITICAL when affected entity remains ERROR
      action: SITE or ACTIVITY according to operation scope
    OPERATION_STALE:
      condition: operation exceeds the authoritative timeout policy used by operation recovery
      severity: WARNING
      action: ACTIVITY
      guard: do not invent a generic timeout when operation type has no policy
  dns:
    DNS_PROVIDER_ERROR:
      condition: configured provider has persisted ERROR state
      severity: WARNING
      action: DNS
    DNS_RECORD_DRIFT:
      condition: background checker confirms mismatch for a Meowbox-managed record in two consecutive checks
      severity: WARNING
      action: DNS
      guard: timeout, rate limit or provider outage yields source UNAVAILABLE, not drift
  update:
    UPDATE_FAILED:
      condition: latest panel update attempt is terminal failed and no later successful attempt exists
      severity: WARNING when panel is operational, CRITICAL when maintenance or health state remains degraded
      action: UPDATES
    UPDATE_BLOCKED:
      condition: authoritative update-readiness contract reports blocked with a safe reason code
      severity: WARNING
      action: UPDATES
      guard: disabled until updater reliability work exposes a stable readiness contract
  source:
    DATA_SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE:
      condition: a required source cannot be read and no fresh cached value exists
      severity: WARNING, CRITICAL only when the unavailable source is required to establish basic server safety
      action: relevant destination or null

diagnostics:
  architecture:
    service: DashboardDiagnosticsService
    behavior:
      - refreshes diagnostics on scheduler ticks, never during dashboard request
      - one in-flight refresh per selected local server process
      - retains last successful value with observedAt and error state
      - clears stale values only after preserving explicit last-known timestamp
      - starts with Unknown after API restart until the first refresh
  budgets:
    core_services:
      interval_seconds: 30
      timeout_seconds: 5
    nginx_validation:
      interval_seconds: 60
      timeout_seconds: 10
    nginx_drift:
      interval_seconds: 300
      timeout_seconds: 30
    pm2:
      interval_seconds: 60
      timeout_seconds: 20
    dns:
      interval_seconds: 600
      timeout_seconds_per_provider: 10
      max_concurrency: 3
      backoff: exponential, capped at 60 minutes
  nginx_drift:
    expected_manifest:
      - refactor current config generators into pure render functions before comparing
      - manifest contains allowlisted absolute path, SHA-256 and owning entity ID
      - include only files whose lifecycle Meowbox owns
      - include custom user configuration only as input to canonical rendered managed files
    agent_response:
      - path identifier
      - exists boolean
      - actual SHA-256 or null
      - no file contents
    safety:
      - Agent rejects paths outside explicit managed config roots
      - comparison never rewrites a file
      - unknown extra files are ignored in first release
  dns_drift:
    scope:
      - only enabled configured providers
      - only records explicitly managed by Meowbox
      - compare canonicalized record name, type, value, priority and proxied state where supported
    consistency:
      - require two consecutive mismatches to avoid provider propagation false positives
      - honor provider TTL and rate limits
      - cache safe reason codes, never provider response bodies
  pm2:
    scope:
      - root Meowbox processes
      - configured site Node processes only
    scaling:
      - add one bounded Agent diagnostic request instead of one request per site
      - inspect only users/domains with an expected PM2 process contract
      - concurrency is at most 2 per-site PM2 daemon reads
      - large inventories are processed across ticks and report partial coverage
    grace:
      - suppress missing or stopped warnings while related deploy/start/stop operation is active
      - use operation timestamps and type-specific recovery policy

api:
  endpoint:
    method: GET
    path: /dashboard/overview
    auth: authenticated ADMIN or MANAGER
    response: DashboardOverview contractVersion 1
  old_endpoint:
    path: /dashboard/summary
    policy: keep unchanged for one compatibility release
    removal: only after supported remote-server upgrade floor guarantees overview v1
  request_behavior:
    - create one correlation ID
    - read current user ID and role
    - execute independent source loaders with Promise.allSettled
    - normalize each source into a typed section
    - compute Problems after all available source results settle
    - return partial snapshot with per-section source state
  error_behavior:
    - 401 for unauthenticated requests
    - 403 only when role is unsupported, not for a MANAGER with zero sites
    - 200 with partial source states for recoverable section failures
    - 500 only when the top-level response cannot be formed safely
  headers:
    Cache-Control: private, no-store
    X-Dashboard-Contract: 1
  limits:
    problems: 100
    sites: 8
    activeOperations: 5
    services: 8
    activity: 8
    recentFailureLookbackHours: 24

backend_design:
  DashboardOverviewService:
    responsibility:
      - orchestrate bounded source loaders
      - enforce user scope
      - produce one generatedAt timestamp
      - call problem detector registry
      - serialize shared contract
    forbidden:
      - system commands
      - external network access
      - state mutation
  DashboardQueryService:
    responsibility:
      - aggregate sites, domains, certificates, backups, operations, sessions and activity
      - use set-based queries with limits and selected fields
      - keep all role predicates explicit
    query_rules:
      - do not load full backup histories
      - use grouped counts and latest-per-entity queries
      - avoid Promise.all over entity collections
      - select no encrypted credential, command, raw output or metadata payload fields
      - use one generatedAt cutoff consistently across queries
  DashboardProblemDetectorRegistry:
    responsibility:
      - register pure detectors by source category
      - isolate detector exceptions
      - enforce deterministic IDs and sorting
      - sanitize all messages through shared safeErrorMessage policy
  DashboardDiagnosticsService:
    responsibility:
      - own cached command and external-provider diagnostic state
      - expose snapshots synchronously to overview service
      - publish freshness and support capability
  MonitoringService_changes:
    - preserve latest Agent collectedAt, uptime, hostname, load, CPU count, all disks and normalized network rates
    - reject non-finite and negative values according to metric semantics
    - retain a bounded ring buffer only for real sparklines if existing history query is insufficient
  operation_changes:
    - add bounded internal query for recent and active operations scoped by user
    - do not create an unrestricted public list endpoint unless another screen needs it
  status_provider_changes:
    - distinguish installed, expected-running, stopped, failed and unavailable
    - cache command results outside request path
    - never mark an absent optional database engine as failed

database_query_plan:
  required_patterns:
    sites:
      - grouped counts by Site.status under role scope
      - bounded priority list ordered by error and updatedAt
    domains:
      - grouped appStatus counts and domain totals
      - bounded error rows joined to owned sites
    health:
      - aggregate recent HealthCheckPing per domain in the database
      - return sampled count with percentage
      - no samples maps to Unknown
    backups:
      - union or separately aggregate Backup, ServerPathBackup and PanelDataBackup
      - latest-per-target query is set-based
      - coverage query joins enabled per-site configs and applicable global schedules
    ssl:
      - aggregate explicit status and expiresAt thresholds
      - select only nearest expirations and errors
    operations:
      - query active states plus bounded recent terminal failures
    activity:
      - select last eight safe fields only
    security:
      - count failed logins in a bounded timestamp range
      - count active sessions without loading session rows
  index_gate:
    - capture EXPLAIN QUERY PLAN for production-like fixture
    - use existing status, site, domain and timestamp indexes first
    - if a full scan remains material, add the narrowest index through prisma migrate dev
    - never use db push
    - index migration must be isolated, reversible and benchmarked for write cost

frontend_design:
  page_shell:
    file: web/pages/index.vue
    responsibility:
      - page title and selected-server context
      - compose dashboard components
      - no detector or API-shape business logic
  composable:
    file: web/composables/useDashboardOverview.ts
    responsibility:
      - fetch selected-server overview
      - validate contract version
      - preserve last successful snapshot during refresh
      - abort request when server changes or component unmounts
      - prevent overlapping polls
      - pause polling while document.hidden
      - refresh immediately on visibility restore and selected-server change
      - expose initialLoading, refreshing, lastSuccessAt and top-level error
    polling_seconds: 30
  socket_metrics:
    rule: apply a newer Agent metrics event only when it belongs to the same selected server and passes validation
    fallback: overview resource snapshot remains authoritative when socket is unavailable
  component_boundaries:
    - web/components/dashboard/DashboardServerPulse.vue
    - web/components/dashboard/DashboardProblemsInbox.vue
    - web/components/dashboard/DashboardResourceStrip.vue
    - web/components/dashboard/DashboardSitesPanel.vue
    - web/components/dashboard/DashboardRuntimePanel.vue
    - web/components/dashboard/DashboardProtectionPanel.vue
    - web/components/dashboard/DashboardSecurityPanel.vue
    - web/components/dashboard/DashboardActivityPanel.vue
    - web/components/dashboard/DashboardSectionState.vue
  boundary_rule: create cohesive operational panels, not one component per number or icon
  navigation_registry:
    responsibility: map DashboardProblemAction.target and entityId to existing internal routes
    security:
      - exhaustive switch over action target enum
      - reject unknown target
      - validate entity ID as opaque route param
      - never evaluate server-provided path or URL

data_states:
  initial_loading:
    - render structural skeletons matching final panel geometry
    - do not render zero counters
  background_refresh:
    - keep existing data visible
    - mark refresh in pulse without blocking interaction
    - apply response only if request server key still equals selected server key
  partial_failure:
    - render healthy sections normally
    - render failed section with Unavailable label, safe message and retry through global refresh
    - create source Problem only when source is required
  total_failure:
    - keep last successful snapshot marked Stale if it belongs to same selected server
    - otherwise render selected-server offline or unavailable state
  empty:
    - zero owned sites is a real empty state
    - zero Problems is healthy only when required coverage is OK
  stale:
    - display data age
    - do not advance uptime locally past the last observed value without marking it derived

multi_server_compatibility:
  server_switch:
    - key all cached snapshots by selected server ID
    - never reuse one server snapshot for another server
    - cancel old request and socket association before applying new data
  capability_detection:
    preferred: GET /dashboard/overview returns X-Dashboard-Contract 1
    legacy: 404 or unsupported contract marks overviewV1 false
    forbidden: treat 401, 403, timeout or 500 as legacy support failure
  legacy_adapter:
    inputs:
      - GET /dashboard/summary
      - GET /system/metrics
      - GET /sites
    outputs:
      - only fields whose legacy meaning is trustworthy
      - all unsupported Problems and diagnostics explicitly marked UNSUPPORTED
      - compatibility notice with action to open server updates for ADMIN
    restrictions:
      - no fake disks or network values from absent fields
      - no synthesis of healthy state from empty legacy arrays
      - no manager data if legacy endpoint returns 403
    lifespan: remove after one documented minimum-version compatibility window

security:
  response_minimization:
    - exclude encrypted fields, provider configs, tokens, passwords, command text and raw outputs
    - exclude absolute filesystem paths from Problems and compact activity
    - use safe labels rather than database metadata blobs
  errors:
    - pass source failures through safeErrorMessage with 240-character maximum
    - redact URL credentials, query secrets, bearer tokens and provider response bodies
    - log detailed server-side correlation separately without returning it
  authorization:
    - enforce role and ownership on every query
    - test mixed-owner data fixtures
    - action availability follows destination authorization
  request_safety:
    - GET is side-effect free and private no-store
    - polling rate remains below configured throttling budget
    - diagnostic scheduler applies timeouts, backoff and concurrency caps
  future_remediation_contract:
    prerequisite: separate approved implementation after read-only inbox proves detector quality
    requirements:
      - server-side allowlisted action ID, never arbitrary command
      - POST endpoint with role and ownership check
      - explicit preflight and human-readable impact
      - confirmation for restart, reissue, retry or config regeneration
      - idempotency key
      - Operation row and audit log
      - bounded timeout and rollback or safe retry semantics
      - action disabled while conflicting Operation is active

accessibility:
  semantic_structure:
    - one h1 and ordered h2 section headings
    - Problems use a list; activity and site summaries use semantic list or table according to viewport
    - links remain links and buttons remain buttons
  keyboard:
    - every action reachable in logical order
    - visible focus uses existing high-contrast focus token
    - dialog traps focus, closes with Escape and restores trigger focus
  screen_reader:
    - icons are decorative when adjacent text exists
    - progress bars expose name, current value, minimum and maximum
    - status changes are not announced on every 30-second poll
    - manual refresh result and newly increased critical count use a polite live region
  contrast:
    - meet WCAG AA for text and controls in dark and light themes
    - status text remains readable without relying on low-opacity color
  localization:
    - user-visible strings remain Russian in current product language
    - date, duration, bytes and rate formatting use shared formatters
    - machine error strings are not exposed untranslated

performance_and_scale:
  response_caps:
    problems: 100
    sites: 8
    operations: 5
    services: 8
    activity: 8
    metric_history_points_per_series: 60
  database:
    - query count must not increase when fixture grows from 10 to 10000 sites
    - select only serialized fields
    - use timestamp cutoffs and indexed order before limit
    - parse JSON only for bounded selected rows
  diagnostics:
    - never scan arbitrary filesystem trees
    - compare a bounded expected manifest
    - spread large PM2 inventories over scheduler ticks
    - use single-flight refresh to prevent thundering herds
  web:
    - one overview request per active visible tab per 30 seconds
    - no concurrent refresh from timer, focus and manual action
    - no expensive deep watcher over full snapshot
    - list keys use deterministic IDs
    - real sparklines render bounded SVG points without chart dependency

observability:
  api_metrics:
    - dashboard_overview_duration_ms by role and local_or_proxy
    - dashboard_overview_partial_failure_total by source
    - dashboard_problem_count by code and severity without entity labels
    - dashboard_diagnostic_duration_ms by diagnostic
    - dashboard_diagnostic_failure_total by diagnostic and safe reason code
  logs:
    - one structured completion line with correlation ID, duration, role, section states and problem counts
    - no per-site success log
    - detector failure includes detector code and correlation ID
  web_telemetry:
    - contract unsupported
    - full refresh failure
    - section unavailable
    - no metric values or entity names in client telemetry

implementation_phases:
  P00_contract_and_fixture:
    objective: freeze semantics before visual rewrite
    tasks:
      - add shared DashboardOverview v1 types and enums
      - create representative ADMIN and MANAGER fixtures
      - include healthy, critical, partial-source, empty and legacy fixtures
      - add response-size assertion
    exit:
      - shared package builds
      - fixtures compile against shared contract
      - action target mapping is exhaustive

  P01_query_and_snapshot:
    objective: replace current N+1 summary with bounded consistent read model
    tasks:
      - add DashboardQueryService
      - implement role-scoped aggregate queries
      - aggregate real HealthCheckPing samples and preserve Unknown
      - add active and recent operation internal query
      - normalize monitoring source without losing disk, network, uptime or load fields
      - expose GET /dashboard/overview
      - keep old summary endpoint unchanged
    exit:
      - no query loop depends on site count
      - MANAGER cannot observe another owner data
      - partial source failure returns valid contract

  P02_core_problem_detectors:
    objective: ship trusted Problems Inbox coverage from existing authoritative state
    codes:
      - AGENT_OFFLINE
      - METRICS_STALE
      - DISK_USAGE_WARNING
      - DISK_USAGE_CRITICAL
      - SITE_ERROR
      - DOMAIN_APPLICATION_ERROR
      - SITE_UNAVAILABLE
      - BACKUP_LATEST_FAILED
      - BACKUP_COVERAGE_GAP
      - BACKUP_OVERDUE
      - BACKUP_REPOSITORY_CHECK_FAILED
      - SSL_ERROR
      - SSL_EXPIRED
      - SSL_EXPIRING_CRITICAL
      - SSL_EXPIRING_WARNING
      - SSL_EXPECTED_BUT_UNKNOWN
      - OPERATION_RECENTLY_FAILED
      - OPERATION_STALE
      - DNS_PROVIDER_ERROR
      - UPDATE_FAILED
    tasks:
      - implement pure detector registry
      - centralize thresholds and schedule grace rules
      - sanitize every summary
      - add deterministic sorting and deduplication
    exit:
      - each detector has positive, negative, boundary and unavailable-source tests
      - zero-source input cannot report HEALTHY

  P03_dashboard_ui:
    objective: replace current card wall with operations-first layout
    tasks:
      - implement useDashboardOverview composable
      - implement pulse, inbox, resources and operational panels
      - remove standalone quick-actions card
      - place create-site action in pulse and contextual links in panels
      - add loading, stale, unavailable, unsupported and empty states
      - add legacy selected-server adapter and compatibility notice
      - replace fake or absent metrics with authoritative fields only
      - split index.vue into cohesive components
    exit:
      - uptime and Problems Inbox are above fold in reference viewports
      - no unbounded list renders
      - server switch cannot display mislabeled stale data

  P04_cached_system_diagnostics:
    objective: add reliable service, PM2 and Nginx coverage without slowing GET
    tasks:
      - add DashboardDiagnosticsService scheduler cache
      - move service status commands out of dashboard request path
      - add installed and expected-state semantics
      - add bounded PM2 diagnostic Agent contract
      - refactor Nginx managed renderers to pure output where required
      - add Nginx validation and managed-file checksum comparison
      - enable CORE_SERVICE_INACTIVE, PM2_PROCESS_UNHEALTHY, PM2_PROCESS_MISSING, NGINX_CONFIG_INVALID and NGINX_MANAGED_CONFIG_DRIFT
    exit:
      - dashboard GET runs zero commands
      - diagnostic timeout preserves partial overview
      - drift test compares hashes without returning file content

  P05_cached_dns_diagnostics:
    objective: add low-noise DNS drift coverage
    tasks:
      - define canonical managed-record comparison
      - run provider probes in background with rate limits and backoff
      - require two consecutive mismatches
      - expose coverage and source freshness
      - enable DNS_RECORD_DRIFT
    exit:
      - provider outage never becomes drift
      - dashboard request performs no provider call
      - no provider secret or raw response is stored in diagnostic cache

  P06_quality_and_rollout:
    objective: prove behavior under production-like conditions
    tasks:
      - run accessibility keyboard and screen-reader checks
      - run dark, light, desktop, tablet and mobile visual review
      - run 10000-site query-count and response-size fixture
      - test selected current, legacy, offline and permission-denied remote servers
      - measure local and proxied latency budgets
      - deploy through dev-mode workflow without make update
      - observe one full diagnostics interval before release decision
    exit:
      - all acceptance criteria pass
      - rollback remains code-only
      - operator signs off information hierarchy and issue wording

  P07_safe_remediation_followup:
    objective: convert selected navigation actions into audited safe operations
    status: separate task after detector false-positive audit
    candidate_actions:
      - retry failed backup
      - open certificate reissue confirmation
      - restart an expected-running failed service
      - regenerate confirmed drifted managed Nginx config after diff preview
    forbidden_initial_actions:
      - automatic disk cleanup
      - arbitrary shell command
      - automatic DNS overwrite
      - panel update start
      - bulk restart

file_plan:
  create:
    - shared/src/dashboard.ts
    - api/src/dashboard/dashboard-overview.service.ts
    - api/src/dashboard/dashboard-query.service.ts
    - api/src/dashboard/dashboard-problems.ts
    - api/src/dashboard/dashboard-diagnostics.service.ts
    - api/test/dashboard-overview.test.js
    - api/test/dashboard-problems.test.js
    - web/composables/useDashboardOverview.ts
    - web/components/dashboard/DashboardServerPulse.vue
    - web/components/dashboard/DashboardProblemsInbox.vue
    - web/components/dashboard/DashboardResourceStrip.vue
    - web/components/dashboard/DashboardSitesPanel.vue
    - web/components/dashboard/DashboardRuntimePanel.vue
    - web/components/dashboard/DashboardProtectionPanel.vue
    - web/components/dashboard/DashboardSecurityPanel.vue
    - web/components/dashboard/DashboardActivityPanel.vue
    - web/components/dashboard/DashboardSectionState.vue
    - web/tests/dashboard-overview-contract.test.js
  modify:
    - shared/src/index.ts
    - api/src/dashboard/dashboard.controller.ts
    - api/src/dashboard/dashboard.module.ts
    - api/src/dashboard/dashboard.service.ts
    - api/src/monitoring/monitoring.service.ts
    - web/pages/index.vue
    - web/assets/global.css only for reusable dashboard tokens missing from current system
  conditional:
    - api/src/agent/agent-relay service files for bounded diagnostics events
    - agent/src/agent.service.ts for Nginx, PM2 and checksum diagnostic handlers
    - api/package.json and api/package-lock.json for direct cron dependency
    - shared Agent event types when diagnostics contract is added
  decomposition_rule:
    - do not keep old and new business logic duplicated
    - keep legacy response adapter isolated and deletion-ready
    - do not split trivial presentation into shallow one-use helpers

testing:
  shared:
    - TypeScript build verifies discriminated unions and exhaustive actions
  backend_contract:
    - ADMIN full snapshot
    - MANAGER owned-site snapshot
    - MANAGER with zero sites
    - mixed-owner leakage regression
    - partial DataSource failure
    - invalid metric normalization
    - response list and byte caps
    - no write call during GET
  detector_matrix:
    - exact threshold minus one, exact threshold and threshold plus one
    - stale and unavailable source
    - deterministic ID and sort
    - duplicate source record
    - safe truncation and secret redaction
    - active operation suppression
    - zero HealthCheckPing samples
    - intentionally stopped site and optional service
    - backup schedule timezone, invalid cron and grace
    - DNS first mismatch, second mismatch and provider failure
  query_scale:
    - compare query count for 10 and 10000 sites
    - verify latest backup query does not grow per site
    - inspect query plans for status and timestamp filters
    - assert bounded selected columns exclude secret fields
  diagnostics:
    - single-flight under simultaneous ticks
    - timeout and stale cache behavior
    - Agent disconnect during probe
    - Nginx allowlisted path rejection
    - hash mismatch without file-content transfer
    - PM2 large inventory partial coverage
    - DNS rate limit and exponential backoff
  web_contract:
    - v1 response renders all source states
    - unknown contract version fails closed
    - 404 triggers legacy adapter; 401, 403 and 500 do not
    - selected-server race discards old response
    - polling pauses hidden and never overlaps
    - previous same-server data remains visible during refresh
    - action target registry rejects unknown values
  web_accessibility:
    - keyboard order and visible focus
    - dialog focus restoration
    - status has text independent of color
    - progress values expose accessible labels
    - reduced motion
  visual_matrix:
    widths: [320, 390, 768, 1024, 1440]
    themes: [dark, light]
    data_states: [healthy, critical, many_problems, partial, loading, empty, legacy, offline]
  verification_commands:
    - cd shared && npm run build
    - cd api && npm run build
    - cd api && TS_NODE_TRANSPILE_ONLY=1 node --test -r ts-node/register -r ../tools/register-shared-source.js test/dashboard-overview.test.js test/dashboard-problems.test.js
    - cd web && npm run test:contracts
    - cd web && npx nuxi typecheck
    - cd web && npm run build
    - cd agent && npm run build when Agent diagnostics change

acceptance:
  AC01:
    given: ADMIN opens current selected server at 1440x900
    then: selected server, overall state, uptime, Agent, version, refresh age and Problems Inbox are visible without scrolling
  AC02:
    given: mobile viewport 390x844
    then: server identity, overall state, uptime and Problems Inbox entry point are visible in first viewport without horizontal scroll
  AC03:
    given: at least one critical and one warning Problem
    then: critical appears first and every item shows severity text, entity, safe summary, age and allowlisted action
  AC04:
    given: zero confirmed Problems and all required sources OK
    then: inbox renders compact No confirmed problems state
  AC05:
    given: zero Problems and one required source unavailable
    then: overall state is UNKNOWN and UI does not claim the server is healthy
  AC06:
    given: metrics source lacks disk or network
    then: UI renders Unknown or Unsupported and never zero percent or zero bytes as fact
  AC07:
    given: a domain has zero real HealthCheckPing samples
    then: availability is Unknown and not 100 percent
  AC08:
    given: one dashboard source throws
    then: endpoint returns valid partial overview and unrelated sections remain usable
  AC09:
    given: 10000 sites and 50000 domains fixture
    then: response lists respect caps, payload is at most 128 KiB and query count is unchanged from small fixture
  AC10:
    given: MANAGER owns one of two users sites
    then: response contains only owned entities and no ADMIN-only infrastructure, security, DNS or update data
  AC11:
    given: user selects another server while request is in flight
    then: old response is discarded and never rendered under new server name
  AC12:
    given: selected server returns overview 404
    then: trusted legacy sections render with compatibility notice and unsupported diagnostics are explicit
  AC13:
    given: selected server returns 401, 403 or 500
    then: Web does not misclassify it as a LegacyServer
  AC14:
    given: tab is hidden for five minutes
    then: no polling occurs while hidden and one non-overlapping refresh occurs after visibility returns
  AC15:
    given: dashboard GET is called repeatedly
    then: no DB write, system command, Agent diagnostic request, provider request or notification dispatch occurs in request path
  AC16:
    given: optional PostgreSQL or MariaDB is not installed and not required
    then: it is neutral and does not produce CORE_SERVICE_INACTIVE
  AC17:
    given: site is intentionally STOPPED
    then: STOPPED alone does not produce a Problem
  AC18:
    given: expected service or PM2 process is inactive during matching active operation grace
    then: detector suppresses transient Problem until grace expires
  AC19:
    given: Nginx managed file hash differs
    then: Problem appears from cached diagnostic without transferring content or changing the file
  AC20:
    given: external DNS provider times out
    then: DNS source becomes unavailable and DNS_RECORD_DRIFT is not emitted
  AC21:
    given: first confirmed DNS mismatch
    then: no drift Problem appears until a second consecutive check confirms it
  AC22:
    given: source error includes credential-bearing URL or token-like value
    then: response contains only redacted summary at or below 240 characters
  AC23:
    given: keyboard-only user
    then: all dashboard actions and Problems dialog work with visible focus and logical order
  AC24:
    given: prefers-reduced-motion
    then: non-essential dashboard motion is disabled
  AC25:
    given: first dashboard release is rolled back
    then: old Web and API continue because no schema, env, filesystem-layout or OS-state migration was required

rollout:
  pre_implementation:
    - preserve unrelated dirty worktree changes
    - capture current dashboard screenshots in dark and light themes for comparison
    - record current overview request count, payload and latency baseline
  development:
    - implement phases in order; do not begin mutating remediation work
    - verify each phase against fixtures before wiring the next
    - use current VPS dev-mode workflow and preserve /opt/meowbox/.dev-mode
    - never run make update on current VPS
  release_candidate:
    - test one current local server
    - test one current selected remote server
    - test one LegacyServer
    - test offline selected server
    - observe diagnostic scheduler CPU, memory, command duration and provider rate limits
  release:
    - bump VERSION before commit, tag and release
    - ship overview contract and compatibility adapter together
    - keep legacy endpoint for one compatibility window
    - monitor partial failures, latency and Problem code distribution
  rollback:
    - roll back code release only
    - leave no dashboard-owned persistent rows
    - retain old summary endpoint until rollback window closes

migration_gate:
  planned_answers:
    prisma_schema_changed: false
    nginx_php_fpm_logrotate_cron_systemd_templates_changed: false in P00 through P03
    server_files_or_directories_moved: false
    new_env_variable: false
    operating_system_state_changed: false
  consequence: no migration required for first dashboard release
  diagnostics_note: >
    P04 refactors read-only rendering and adds Agent diagnostics but must not regenerate
    existing configs or alter OS state. If implementation changes a managed template or
    installed unit, it becomes a separate system migration with idempotent regeneration.
  index_note: >
    Any Prisma index added after query-plan evidence requires prisma migrate dev and an
    isolated reversible migration. Never use db push.

risks:
  R01:
    risk: too many detectors create noise and destroy trust
    mitigation: ship core evidence-backed detectors first; audit false positives before enabling diagnostics extensions
  R02:
    risk: dashboard probes overload Agent, PM2 or DNS providers
    mitigation: out-of-request scheduler, cache, single-flight, concurrency caps, backoff and partial coverage
  R03:
    risk: source outage is shown as healthy
    mitigation: explicit source state and UNKNOWN overall derivation
  R04:
    risk: MANAGER receives global data
    mitigation: role-scoped loaders, mixed-owner tests and no fetch-then-filter behavior
  R05:
    risk: new Web breaks older selected servers
    mitigation: contract header, strict legacy classification and temporary adapter
  R06:
    risk: Nginx drift comparison reports user-managed files
    mitigation: compare only canonical Meowbox-owned manifest paths and ignore unknown extras
  R07:
    risk: DNS propagation causes false drift
    mitigation: canonicalization, TTL awareness and two consecutive mismatches
  R08:
    risk: status polling creates command storm
    mitigation: cached diagnostics and zero commands in GET path
  R09:
    risk: backup overdue calculation disagrees with scheduler timezone
    mitigation: one explicit cron helper and the same server timezone contract used by scheduler and detector
  R10:
    risk: dashboard redesign hides useful current data
    mitigation: current-state inventory, fixture matrix and operator visual sign-off before replacement
  R11:
    risk: one-click fixes make incidents worse
    mitigation: first release navigation-only; mutating remediation requires separate audited Operation contract
  R12:
    risk: plan becomes coupled to updater migration refactor
    mitigation: show UPDATE_FAILED now; keep UPDATE_BLOCKED unsupported until authoritative updater readiness exists

delivery_definition:
  complete_when:
    - P00 through P06 are implemented and all acceptance criteria pass
    - operator approves desktop and mobile information hierarchy
    - dashboard endpoint is bounded, role-safe and side-effect free
    - Problems Inbox reports core and supported cached diagnostics without false healthy states
    - current and legacy selected-server flows are verified
    - production release and rollback notes are prepared
  not_complete_when:
    - only CSS and card order changed
    - Problems are hardcoded in Vue
    - metrics silently fall back to zero
    - dashboard still performs per-site backup queries
    - dashboard GET triggers system or provider probes
    - ADMIN-only response is reused for MANAGER
    - unsafe remediation mutations are added without Operation, audit, preflight and idempotency

open_questions: []
